            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0601" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10445: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-18T16:00:00+08:00">May 18, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 18—2:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>400. 1. Following from American Consul at Swatow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“May 17, 4 p.m. Kwangsi adherents evacuating Swatow hurriedly. … Due to
                            the possibility of disorders during the period of transition…, I request
                            the presence of an American warship, if one be available.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. Message has been repeated to commander in chief United States Asiatic Fleet
                    with my concurrence in request.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
